// QC: Better Immersion to Baldur's Gate - BG0300
// Translation strings extracted from bg0300_baldurs_gate.d; original English preserved.

@1 = ~Bother me no longer.~
@2 = ~I come here every single day to pray to Ilmater. He grants me some bonuses to armor class. Oh... you don't get it, do you. I'll just stop talking.~
@3 = ~I'm sending my kid to school soon. I want him to become a Priest of Helm. My wife believes kobolds are refused Helm's blessing but in my eyes it's the intention that matters, not race.~
@4 = ~Undercellar gained it's reputation by being a den filled with vice, crime, and illicit commerce. I heard that it connects with the sewers and smugglers use them to traffic stolen goods illegally. Thieves, opium sellers and other scum of earth.~
@5 = ~How come no one shut it down?~
@6 = ~Gold, blood, and the hypocrisy of the high-and-mighty, my friend. This whole city’s rotten from the top down. Hierarchy is complex. You’ve got the Grand Dukes at the peak, then the Flaming Fist and the Watch, the wealthy nobility, the merchant coin-clippers, us common folk, and finally the destitute dregs sleeping in the gutters. As a hobgoblin? I’m squeezed somewhere near the bottom, depending on how big of a bribe the local guardsmen want that day.~
@7 = ~Many of those 'noble' rich crowd are the Undercellar's finest customers. They use their coin to ensure the Flaming Fist looks the other way. Then you’ve got the Thieves' Guild keeping order down there. They contain the worst butchery underground so it doesn't spill onto the streets. The Fist tolerates this 'controlled crime' because a total shutdown would turn the city into a war zone. I hate to admit it, but crime keeps the peace around here and encourages the Flaming Fist to work in the first place.~
@8 = ~Besides, the place is a labyrinth with dozens of holes bleeding into the sewers. A full-scale raid by the Fist would be needlessly dangerous. They'd lose dozens of men to traps and cornered cutthroats, and the real targets would just slip away in the dark anyway. I’ve no love for the Fist, but their deaths would only leave the rest of us unprotected. It’s simply not worth the blood.~
@9 = ~I see. Thanks for the insight.~
@10 = ~Name's Bemley. You're welcome. Tread carefully.~
@11 = ~No time to talk. I have laundry to do.~
@12 = ~I have nothing more to say to you.~
@13 = ~Good day, friends. I hope you'll have a nice day.~
@14 = ~Alora! Darling, I was just thinking about you. I see you made some friends.~
@15 = ~Good day, friends. I hope you'll have a nice day.~
@16 = ~Not too shabby. I was late again with paying taxes this month and Flaming Fist is right on my arse. Having no employment is as soul-sucking as death itself. Would you mind borrowing me some money? I... am afraid I won't be able to pay you back but since you're Alora's pals It'd be a kind thing to do.~
@17 = ~Alora's friends are my friends. Here you go. 300 gold coins.~
@18 = ~We don't have any money. We're sorry.~
@19 = ~I don't know you. If I parted with my money with every beggar I met, I'd have less than none.~
@20 = ~That's more like it. Alora, my dear, you found some meritorious gals. I'm almost jealous. Thank you so much, my friend. I won't forget it.~
@21 = ~This is most sorrowful news. Looks like we both hit the rock bottom. Well, we should all start digging deeper through people's stashes. Homes around here are filled with gems and money to the brim. Take care, Alora.~
@22 = ~It's okay, Alora. I expected as much from a band of barbarians such as this. Alora, take care of yourself. And you? May you get run over by a speeding horse-pulled carriage.~
@23 = ~Adan! I'm so glad to see you. This is <CHARNAME>. Adan is my friend and fellow busybody. How is life treating you?~
@24 = ~So this is what you're like? I was expecting more altruism from you. Lying that you have no money is one thing but straight up insulting someone for no particular reason is immoral and just... wrong. I hope you keep that in mind next time we encounter someone who might need our help.~
@25 = ~This fair is nothing compared to Nashkel's infamous Carnival. I should visit one day. Now, that the city is open again I can make a trip.~
